QRF was consistently less robust than RF on every external data set (Additional file~\ref{app:noise:sec:rf_vs_qrf_assay}). As seen with QM9, choice of molecular representation has a minimal effect on noise robustness across all three external datasets, reinforcing the finding that model architecture, not representation, is the main driver of noise robustness. 

